-- REJECTED (R1, §8.1). The witness for smucclaw/l4-ide#958.
--
-- `the base` and `the top` are @export'd, so R1 emits each as a Catala SCOPE.
-- `the middle` is not, so it is emitted as a toplevel `declaration … equals` —
-- and its call to `the base` becomes `output of TheBase with { … }`, which
-- Catala allows only inside a scope body. The emitted module is not valid
-- Catala: `catala typecheck` rejects it with "Scope calls are not allowed
-- outside of a scope" (catala 1.2.1, exit 123).
--
-- Until the refusal this file pins, `l4 catala` emitted that module, printed
-- nothing at all on stderr, and exited 0 — the invalid output was discovered
-- only by running Catala over it by hand.
--
-- `l4 check` reports this file as clean; nothing but the Catala lowering
-- catches it, which is why it is a fixture. The fix an author wants is to mark
-- `the middle` @export too: the hatch is all-or-nothing along the chain, and
-- `../export-chain.l4` is the same shape with every rung exported.

§ `Chain`

@export
GIVEN n IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the base` n MEANS n TIMES 2

GIVEN n IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the middle` n MEANS `the base` n PLUS 1

@export
GIVEN n IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the top` n MEANS `the middle` n PLUS 10
